Flight SQL server that executes queries against a shared governed session.



Every handler requires the authenticated typestate evidence that the

authentication layer attaches, and authorizes through its

[`QueryPolicy`]. There is no construction without a policy:



```compile_fail

use flightdeck_core::governed::GovernedSession;

use flightdeck_server::service::QueryService;

use std::time::Duration;



// `None` is not a `QueryPolicy`: Flightdeck has no authorization-disabled mode.

let _service = QueryService::new(

GovernedSession::builder(64 << 20).build(),

None,

Duration::from_secs(30),

Duration::from_secs(300),

);

```



and none over a raw `DataFusion` session, whose SQL could name a path

(`read_parquet('…')`, a URL table, `CREATE EXTERNAL TABLE … LOCATION`)

that authorization never sees:



```compile_fail

# fn policy() -> flightdeck_server::service::QueryPolicy { unimplemented!() }

use flightdeck_server::service::QueryService;

use std::time::Duration;



let _service = QueryService::new(

datafusion::prelude::SessionContext::new(),

policy(),

Duration::from_secs(30),

Duration::from_secs(300),

);

```
